# Project rules for Cursor

- Organization: group code by feature, not by layer or language.
  - src/GameRuntime/Core: plugin entry and orchestration only
  - src/GameRuntime/Monitoring: frame-based monitors (StateMonitor, ActionMonitor)
  - src/GameRuntime/Tracking: high-frequency data capture (ContinuousTracker)
  - src/GameRuntime/PlayerAnalysis: player inspection and report
  - src/GameRuntime/Colliders: collider collection and export
  - src/Python: orchestration and analysis scripts
  - src/Data: IPC signals and generated datasets
  - src/Environment: env and dependency setup
  - src/Documentation: human docs; each module has its own readme.md

- Module docs: every feature directory must contain readme.md explaining:
  - purpose, inputs/outputs, dependencies, and maintenance notes

- File moves: when relocating files, update project files (e.g., csproj) accordingly.

- Paths: prefer Path.Combine nesting for 2-arg overload compatibility.

- Logging: use concise, high-signal logs; avoid noisy loops in Update.

- Indentation/style: preserve existing style; do not reformat unrelated code.